{"seq":2,"slug":"caching-strategies","title":"Caching Strategies","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/ai-llm/ai-cost-latency-optimization/caching-strategies","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"prompt-caching","title":"提示缓存（Prompt Caching）","url":"/l-doc-books/h/ai-llm/ai-cost-latency-optimization/caching-strategies/prompt-caching","wordCount":2483,"readingTime":10},{"seq":2,"slug":"semantic-caching","title":"语义缓存","url":"/l-doc-books/h/ai-llm/ai-cost-latency-optimization/caching-strategies/semantic-caching","wordCount":2372,"readingTime":10},{"seq":3,"slug":"cache-friendly-design","title":"缓存友好的应用设计","url":"/l-doc-books/h/ai-llm/ai-cost-latency-optimization/caching-strategies/cache-friendly-design","wordCount":2452,"readingTime":10}],"introHtml":"<p>缓存是 AI 应用中投入产出比最高的一类优化：提示缓存（prompt caching）在推理层复用已计算的前缀、把重复 token 的成本与首 token 延迟同时压低；语义缓存则在应用层对高重复的问答流量直接复用历史答案。本章依次讲解两类缓存的工作机制、价格结构、失效策略与风险边界，并说明为什么它们的收益高度依赖应用结构——只有把缓存当作一等设计约束、让提示布局与会话路由为命中率而设计，这些优化才能真正兑现。</p>\n"}